---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Read Your Quilt Fabric Shopping Plan"
  description="Understand raw additional length, safety, purchase rounding, Fresh-fabric plan, Pattern says, and Buy now."
  eyebrow="Learn QuiltClarity · Results"
  guideSlug="read-your-shopping-plan"
  guideCategory="start_here"
  previous={{
    href: '/guides/check-pattern-yardage/',
    label: 'Check Pattern Yardage',
  }}
  next={{
    href: '/guides/read-your-cutting-plan/',
    label: 'Read Your Cutting Plan',
  }}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Start with project status</h2><p>
      The status says whether stock covers every cut, additional purchase is
      required, or something remains uncovered. Fix any blocking error before
      using the numbers.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use Buy now at the shop</h2><p>
      Buy now is the remaining bolt purchase after stock allocation, safety, and
      upward shop-increment rounding. No additional purchase means the entered
      stock covers the planned cuts.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Keep comparison concepts separate</h2><dl class="guide-definition-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Pattern says</dt><dd>The external reference you entered.</dd>
      </div><div>
        <dt>Fresh-fabric plan</dt><dd>
          All cuts from new fabric, ignoring stock.
        </dd>
      </div><div>
        <dt>Buy now</dt><dd>The shortfall after owned fabric is used.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Audit raw, buffered, and rounded lengths</h2><p>
      Raw additional plan comes from placement geometry. Safety increases only
      new fabric. Recommended purchase rounds upward to the selected increment.
      These are intentionally different values.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
